there are three ways of inserting an element in list 
1)append
lst = [10, 20, 30]
lst.append(40)

2)insert
lst = [10, 20, 30]
lst.insert(1, 15)

3)extend
lst = [10, 20]
lst.extend([30, 40, 50])

append adds one element at the end 
insert adds an element at a specific position
extend adds multiple elements 

*in append python checks if the list has enough unused space and 
If space is available, it places 40 in the next free slot and if not Python allocates a larger
memory block, copies existing elements, and then adds 40.

*in insert python finds the index and from the index elemts are shifted one position right 
and the new element is placed in the empty spoace and if the memeory is fullresizing may occur.

*in extend python determines how many new elements are coming.
It checks whether sufficient space exists.
If needed, it allocates a larger memory block.
Each element is copied into the list one by one.
